  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is RNA-only PCA with multiprofile avgpool, which substantially outperforms single-profile PCA and transformer aggregation, while image-only ResNet is weak. The key uncertainty is whether a learned RNA encoder can improve on PCA under this best-known profile and aggregation setting. config_005 keeps profile_setting=multiprofile and aggregation=avgpool fixed and changes only the RNA encoder to scvi_n200, isolating the representation effect. This is the best next use of budget because it either confirms PCA is sufficient or identifies a better RNA representation before adding multimodal complexity."
